{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And you shall know with your heart, etc.</b> The verse's intention is that a person should reason with his heart: it is not human nature to reprove and discipline except one's own son, for upon him does one insist when seeing him do evil — whereas one's heart does not stir when seeing the son of one's fellow doing wickedness. And this is from the nature implanted in man, to feel about his son when he does something that ought not be done, and to rebuke him and strike him — which one would not do to someone upon whom one does not insist. So too HaShem — <b>your Elohim disciplines you</b> — meaning that even though the nations commit wickedness and abominations, He does not insist upon them as He insists upon you, by virtue of being your Elohim, whose name of Elohim has been singled out upon you; and therefore He disciplines you for every thing that is not good to do."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:15:56.803270501Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}